node.doctext:
It tooks me a long time to correct this, and I don't see what's wrong with this:
<code>
use strict;
use warnings;
use Data::Dumper;

my $data = {status=>"ok",'message-type'=>"member",'message-version'=>"1.0.0"};
my $result_hr;

unfold_hash($data, $result_hr);
print Dumper $result_hr;

sub unfold_hash {
    my ( $raw_hr, $res_hr ) = @_;
    for my $k ( keys %$raw_hr ) {
            $res_hr->{$k} = $raw_hr->{$k}; 
    }
     print "unfold_hash ", $res_hr ? scalar %$res_hr : 0, "\n";
}
</code>
<p>Here, unfold_hash is rather stupid since it does nothing interesting. But the problem remains:
$result_hr is undef.</p>
<p>To correct this I have to say</p>
<code>
my $result_hr={};
unfold_hash($data, $result_hr);
print Dumper $result_hr;
</code>
Now $result_hr holds the content of $data. How comes that the hash auto vivification is lost if the variable $result_hr is undef ?
<p>Thanks</p>
F.
